  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Promoting Conflict-Affected Coomunity Livelihood in Greater Krdofan</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project planned effect (s) on the target society is that; Conflict-affected community improved access to natural resources, livelihood, food security and enjoy social peace and coexistence. The beneficiaries are both, the host communities (sedentary farmers and herders) affected by conflict and IDPs.
The expected effects for the target group of the Project are (Outcome).
&#x2022;	Outcome1:  Natural resources management mechanisms sustained, through; strengthening management and institutional capacities of community-based organizations and traditional leaders.
&#x2022;	Outcome 2:  Community livelihood system promoted, small scale farmers and livestock herders improved access to appropriate agriculture, animal feeding and awareness sessions.  
&#x2022;	Outcome 3: Innovative Youth led/women initiatives supported with diversified livelihood and peace interventions, small business start-up &#x2013;packages, and income generation activities.  
&#x2022;	Outcome 4: Community Access to Safe and Reliable Water for People drinking and livestock&#x2019;s Watering improved.</narrative>
  </description>
